  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 232 PM MST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nHeading into the long term period, starting on Sunday, ridging noses \nin for the morning hours behind the system that impacted the \nforecast area on Saturday. As we progress into the day on Sunday, by \nthe afternoon hours, the ridge flattens with the upper level flow \nbecoming zonal. This pattern will keep us dry, but a by product will \nbe the increased possibility for strong winds in our known wind \nprones along I-25 and I-80. The 700 mb flow ramps up late Sunday \nwith speeds approaching 50 knots and remains so through the \novernight hours with the flow increasing further through Monday as \nspeeds approach 60 knots by the late afternoon into the evening \nhours. With ample subsidence, negative Omega (GFS), these stronger \nwinds have a good chance of making it down to the surface. As such, \nour in-house guidance indicates up to a 65% chance of high winds at \nArlington/Elk Mountain, around a 40% chance along the I-80 Summit, \nand near 55% chance at Bordeaux for later in the day on Sunday into \nMonday. As we head into Tuesday, conditons look to be relatively \nquiet outside of a two weak shortwaves that will slide through, the \nfirst on Tuesday and another one on Wednesday. These won't bring \nwidespread chances of precipitation but increase the threat across \nthe mountains for the two aforementioned days. Beyond Wednesday, a \ntransient ridge noses back in and controls weather heading into next \nweekend. Switching gears a bit and taking a look at temperatures, \nSunday will start off chilly with lows in the upper teens to low 20s \nand don't expect temperatures to warm much as a cold airmass will be \nin place as highs only climb into the upper 30s to low 40s west of \nthe I-25 corridor and low 40s off to the east. These cooler \ntemperatures are short-lived, as warm air advects into the region, \nhighs will climb back into the 40s west of I-25 and low to mid 50s \neast of the I-25 corridor by Monday. These \"warmer\" temperatures \nwill persist through Wednesday, then look for cooler temperatures to \nreturn at the tail end of next week.",
